      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Rail service began in 1871, and before the 1927 bridge, Wiscasset relied on a railroad ferry across the Kennebec.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wiscasset%2C_Maine",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "From 1972 to 1996, Wiscasset hosted Maine Yankee, the state’s only nuclear power plant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wiscasset%2C_Maine",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Wiscasset’s classic architecture earned 10 buildings a 1936 Historic American Buildings Survey listing and five on the National Register.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wiscasset.gov/206/Historic-Prehistoric-Overview",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Archaeologists have identified several prehistoric sites in Wiscasset, including a shell midden near Cushman Cove.",
